                        @* Section 1 *@
                        <div class="br-section" id="s1">
                            <h2 class="br-h2">1. What is a Forex Position Size Calculator?</h2>
                            <p class="br-p">A <strong>Forex position size calculator</strong> is a tool that tells you exactly how many lots (or units) to trade on a given setup so you risk only a predetermined amount of your account — typically 1% or 2% per trade. Instead of guessing lot sizes or over-trading, you input four values and the calculator outputs the correct position size in seconds.</p>
                            <p class="br-p">The four inputs are: your <strong>account balance</strong>, your <strong>risk percentage</strong> (or fixed dollar amount), the <strong>currency pair</strong> you're trading, and your <strong>stop-loss distance in pips</strong>. The calculator does the rest — including pip value conversion if your account is in a different currency to the pair's quote currency.</p>
