                        @* Section 2 *@
                        <div class="br-section" id="s2">
                            <h2 class="br-h2">2. Why Position Sizing Matters in Forex</h2>
                            <p class="br-p">Most traders focus on finding good entry signals, but position sizing is what separates consistently profitable traders from those who blow accounts. A great entry with the wrong lot size can wipe out weeks of gains in a single trade. Conversely, disciplined position sizing lets you weather a string of losses and still trade the next day.</p>
                            <div class="br-pros-cons">
                                <div class="br-pros">
                                    <div class="br-pros-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check me-2"></i>With Proper Position Sizing</div>
                                    <ul style="margin:0;padding:0 0 0 18px;line-height:2.2;font-size:14px;color:#374151;">
                                        <li>Risk is capped at 1–2% per trade regardless of stop-loss distance</li>
                                        <li>Account grows proportionally — larger balance = larger lots automatically</li>
                                        <li>A 10-trade losing streak costs only 10–20% drawdown</li>
                                        <li>Psychological pressure is reduced — you know your maximum loss</li>
                                        <li>Strategy performance is measured accurately over time</li>
                                        <li>Drawdowns are manageable and recoverable</li>
                                    </ul>
                                </div>
                                <div class="br-cons">
                                    <div class="br-cons-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-xmark me-2"></i>Without Proper Position Sizing</div>
                                    <ul style="margin:0;padding:0 0 0 18px;line-height:2.2;font-size:14px;color:#374151;">
                                        <li>One large loss can erase weeks of small gains</li>
                                        <li>Fixed lot sizing ignores account balance changes</li>
                                        <li>Overleveraging on "high-confidence" setups leads to account blowups</li>
                                        <li>Risk per trade is inconsistent — impossible to evaluate strategy edge</li>
                                        <li>Revenge trading after a big loss compounds the problem</li>
                                        <li>Even a winning strategy can fail with bad position sizing</li>
                                    </ul>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="br-divider"></div>

                        @* Section 3 — Formula *@
                        <div class="br-section" id="s3">
                            <h2 class="br-h2">3. The Position Size Formula Explained</h2>
                            <p class="br-p">The core Forex position size formula is straightforward. Once you understand each variable, you can apply it to any currency pair on any platform.</p>

