                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="br-fact-item">
                                    <div class="br-fact-icon" style="background:#f5f3ff;color:#7c3aed;"><i class="fa-solid fa-layer-group"></i></div>
                                    <div>
                                        <div class="br-fact-key">Position Size (lots)</div>
                                        <div class="br-fact-val">The output — how many standard lots to trade. Multiply by 10 for mini lots or 100 for micro lots.</div>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>

                            <div class="br-callout">
                                <i class="fa-solid fa-lightbulb me-2" style="color:#d97706;"></i>
                                <strong>Account Risk calculation:</strong> Account Risk ($) = Account Balance × (Risk % ÷ 100). For $10,000 at 1% risk: $10,000 × 0.01 = <strong>$100</strong>.
                            </div>
